#: source/installation/building-source.md:1
msgid "Building Nix from Source"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:3
msgid ""
"Nix is built with [Meson](https://mesonbuild.com/). It is broken up into "
"multiple Meson packages, which are optionally combined in a single project "
"using Meson's [subprojects](https://mesonbuild.com/Subprojects.html) feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:6
msgid ""
"There are no mandatory extra steps to the building process: generic Meson "
"installation instructions like [this](https://mesonbuild.com/Quick-guide."
"html#using-meson-as-a-distro-packager) should work."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:18
msgid ""
"The installation path can be specified by passing `-Dprefix=prefix` to "
"`meson setup build`. The default installation directory is `/usr/local`. You "
"can change this to any location you like. You must have write permission to "
"the _prefix_ path."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:23
msgid ""
"Nix keeps its _store_ (the place where packages are stored) in `/nix/store` "
"by default. This can be changed using `-Dlibstore:store-dir=path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:27
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:29
msgid ""
"It is best _not_ to change the Nix store from its default, since doing so "
"makes it impossible to use pre-built binaries from the standard Nixpkgs "
"channels — that is, all packages will need to be built from source."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/building-source.md:34
msgid ""
"Nix keeps state (such as its database and log files) in `/nix/var` by "
"default. This can be changed using `-Dlocalstatedir=path`."
msgstr ""
